295.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> it applies, barely: price and the 50-day are above the 200-day and RSI is under 40. Be careful with it here. Your own record says dip-buying has been weak on DELL and that it is a momentum name.</li><li><strong>Your downside idea:</strong> DELL is on your downside list. The nightly report treats that idea as paused while DELL holds above $340. No play is open or watching on the scorecard.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> the chart supports neither side yet. A close under $340.20 puts the downside back on, with $315.00 and then your $295 next. A close above $421.84 would support the upside.</li><li><strong>Against management:</strong> it disagrees. Management raised every target on Sep 1; price is 37% under its high with the report 12 days away. The chart is waiting for Nov 24 to settle it.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Nov 24 report:</strong> revenue against the $49.0B midpoint, the backlog against $95B, gross margin against 20.9%, and whether the $192.0B and $74B full-year figures move again.</li><li><strong>Memory prices:</strong> Micron's next report (quarter ends around Nov 30; date not found) and TrendForce's first-quarter 2027 price call.</li><li><strong>The $340.20 line:</strong> a close under the 200-day before the report would bring your downside levels back into play.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: results, guidance, backlog, inventory, debt and financing figures (company release copy, 10-Q), voting control and officers (10-K filed March 2026). Thin: call detail; the Nov 24 date beyond Webull; the result of the Texas vote; any named successor; the 10-Q legal note was not read. The whole report is one quarter stale.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://finviz.com/news/387708/dell-technologies-delivers-second-quarter-fiscal-2027-financial-results\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FQ2 release 